 "medium (0.65)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-050"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-076", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-076: Trigger attribution: variance of H1->H2 PPP collapse", "score": 1.101, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPS-076 (0.73)", "request matches RQC:RQC-029 (0.73); FAM:SF-APPS-076 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-029"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Trigger attribution: variance of H1->H2 PPP collapse", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Observable in-game process/usage/shot-selection/lineup/context changes explain suppression triggers beyond RTM.", "observed_result": "RTM (ppp_h1 alone) 32.9% of variance. Usage +0.0%; process+shot-zone +1.7%; lineup +0.0%; context +0.0%. Unexplained 65.4%. Total explained 34.6% (RTM=95% of explained).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Process/usage/lineup/context add ~1.7 pp; residual 65.4% is idiosyncratic noise from small per-half n.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=40963 cells; 12617 triggers", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "B_powered_null", "auto_confidence": "high (0.95)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-070"}, {"rel": "auto_addresses_question", "node": "RQC:RQC-029"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-023", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-023: System BEST vs constrained league mix (non-CUT matchup-specificity test)", "score": 1.1, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPS-023 (0.73)", "request matches RQC:RQC-024 (0.74); FAM:SF-APPS-023 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-024"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "System BEST vs constrained league mix (non-CUT matchup-specificity test)", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Matchup-specific (non-CUT) BEST counters beat a feasibility-weighted league mix that ignores game state.", "observed_result": "All BEST vs mix: 1.481 vs 1.212, gap=+0.269, p=0.0000, n=283. Non-CUT BEST vs mix: 1.216 vs 1.206, gap=+0.010, p=0.1709, n=136. L3_MATCHUP non-CUT: gap=+0.001, p=0.3277, n=47. BEST vs AVOID gap=+0.692, p=0.0000, n=169. 1 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Key non-CUT test gap=+0.010, p=0.1709, n=136; H2H L3 non-CUT gap=+0.001, p=0.3277. Headline A vs B is CUT-driven.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=136 non-CUT; n=47 L3 non-CUT"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-041", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-041: PUTBACK suppression matched-pair isolation (star vs team)", "score": 0.744, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPS-041 (0.74)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "PUTBACK suppression matched-pair isolation (star vs team)", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "Conceding a PUTBACK causally suppresses the next offensive possession after matching on game state.", "observed_result": "TEAM ATT=-0.0038 CI[-0.025,+0.015] perm p=0.890 n_t=15614. STAR ATT=+0.0040 [-0.049,+0.052] p=0.834 n_t=2481. STAR Q4 ATT=-0.1045 [-0.217,+0.010] p=0.032 (gradient does not survive matching as a FINDING).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Raw putback suppression collapses once margin/state is matched; original finding was a score/context confound.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n_treated team=15614, star=2481", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:confounding"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:CONFOUNDING"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF30"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-070", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-070: H1 usage as predictor of H2 suppression (distribution shift)", "score": 0.734, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-029 (0.73); FAM:SF-APPS-070 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-029", "FAM:SF-APPS-076 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPS-070"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "H1 usage as predictor of H2 suppression (distribution shift)", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "First-half reliance on a play type predicts second-half suppression after controlling for H1 PPP / mean reversion.", "observed_result": "Test B: all BH-adjusted null/WEAK (PNR ATT=+0.0313 BH_p=0.0658 WEAK; others NULL). Test C top-1 acc=0.550 vs mean-reversion baseline 0.511 (+0.039) vs most-used 0.239. Test A PULL_UP slope -0.0581 p=0.0030; CUT -0.0917 p [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Matched ATT does not survive BH; predictive lift over mean reversion is only +0.039 (0.550 vs 0.511). Bulk of H2 suppression is RTM.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=8873 team-games; Test C test n=1008"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:RTM_SELECTION"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-039", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-039: Series-level AVOID share vs winning (talent confound)", "score": 0.476, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-103 (0.75); FAM:SF-CHT-039 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-103"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Series-level AVOID share vs winning (talent confound)", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Higher AVOID share predicts losing, independent of team quality.", "observed_result": "Game-level rho=-0.19 p=0.008 (inflated n, team-quality confound). Series-level rho=-0.26 p=0.07 (n=50, underpowered; ~80 series needed for p<0.05). Low AVOID-share bin 52.6% vs 25-50% bin 37.0%.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Series n=50 p=0.07; still confounded by team quality (OKC disciplined and good).", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=50 series; stated need ~80 for p<0.05", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:confounding"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:CONFOUNDING"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-027", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-027: Adaptation quality vs talent as predictor of series wins", "score": 0.462, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-082 (0.73); FAM:SF-APPS-027 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-082"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Adaptation quality vs talent as predictor of series wins", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "pct_ran_BEST - pct_ran_AVOID predicts series wins after controlling for RS net-rating talent.", "observed_result": "corr(talent, adapt)=+0.124. Per-series logistic: talent_diff_z +0.737 p=0.0213; adapt_diff_z +0.328 p=0.2755. Team-in-series cluster: talent p=0.0095, adapt p=0.2449. Univariate adapt beta=+0.311 p=0.1128. LPM: talent +0 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "After talent control adapt p=0.275; n~55 series cannot separate coaching adaptation from roster quality.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=55 series / 110 directions"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:confounding"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:CONFOUNDING"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-058: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "score": 0.46, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-051 (0.73); FAM:SF-APPA-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-051"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Each star's top sequential suppressor is stable across seasons, and some teammate X->Y sequences have large negative premiums.", "observed_result": "2/30 (7%) stable (>=75% same top suppressor): D. Mitchell PUTBACK 75%, L. James POST_UP 75%. Negative: J. Tatum->K. Porzingis DRIVE->SPOT_UP -0.444 n=31; Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 n=31; J. Brown->J. Tatum SPOT_U [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Only 2/30 stars meet the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars x 4 seasons; min n=20/cell", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}], "n_results": 10}

